## Byte-equivalence of the validator

src/model-id.ts:13 holds the same regex literal as the round-2 block in
providers.ts: /^(?!sk-)[A-Za-z0-9_.:~/-]{1,128}$/. src/model-id.ts:19-20
holds the same safeModel body: typeof value === "string" &&
MODEL_ID.test(value) ? value : null. The commit removes that exact block from
providers.ts and adds the import. So key-shaped values fail the (?!sk-)
guard, charset-invalid or over-length values fail the class and the bound,
and both give null. Behavior is unchanged on every log path:

- Chat flow: providers.ts:245, 299, 323, 334 all call the one imported
  safeModel.
- Structured flow: servedModel = safeModel(result.model) at
  structured.ts:223; the error record holds model: safeModel(model) at
  structured.ts:240; the final record holds model: servedModel at
  structured.ts:253, the validated value or null.

